adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added `GroupPermissionsV2` (services/.../GroupPermissionsV2.java), the global manage check is:

```java
@Override
public boolean canManage() {
    if (root.hasOneAdminRole(AdminRoles.MANAGE_USERS)) return true;
    return hasPermission(null, AdminPermissionsSchema.VIEW, AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE);
}
```

Because `hasPermission(...)` returns true if *any* of the provided scopes is granted (it iterates permission scopes and checks `expectedScopes.contains(scope)`), a VIEW-only permission on the all-groups resource-type resource will make `canManage()` true. That would allow operations guarded by `requireManage()` / `canManage()` (e.g., group creation at the collection level) to succeed for principals who only have VIEW. This contradicts `canManage(GroupModel group)`, which correctly requires `AdminPermissionsSchema.MANAGE` only. The new test `testManageAllGroups` grants only `MANAGE`, so it doesn't catch the VIEW-only escalation case.
